  "aboutDmxS1Intro": "DMX512 is a control protocol widely used in the entertainment industry (lighting, effects, dimmers). It's a serial stream (RS-485) that loops a \"frame\" containing up to 512 values. Each value = one channel (0→255).",
  "aboutDmxS1RememberTitle": "To remember",
  "aboutDmxS1RememberB1": "1 DMX universe = 512 channels (slots) numbered 1→512.",
  "aboutDmxS1RememberB2": "A device listens to a start address (e.g. 101) and consumes N channels (depending on its mode).",
  "aboutDmxS1RememberB3": "The controller sends back everything continuously: if you stop transmitting, the devices \"freeze\" (or go into fallback).",
