  "infoSummaryCopy": "INFO - benchmarks in the field\n- USB-C = form, not speed: check the standard.\n- NVMe (M.2) much faster than SATA.\n- DisplayPort/HDMI = standards, but beware of versions/cables.\n- On video servers: storage + GPU + throughput are the basis.",
  "infoChecklistCopy": "INFO - Checklist\n☐ Certified USB-C cables (data/video if required)\n☐ Suitable storage (NVMe if large streams)\n☐ Stable GPU drivers (known version)\n☐ Real resolution/FPS test\n☐ Avoid cheap adapters",
  "infoUsbCriticalTitle": "Critical point",
  "infoUsbCriticalBullet1": "USB-C = connector (shape). It doesn't say how fast.",
  "infoUsbCriticalBullet2": "A USB-C cable can be \"charge only\" and not pass data/video.",
  "infoUsbSpeedTitle": "Speed benchmarks (order of magnitude)",
  "infoUsbSpeedBullet1": "USB 2.0: slow (keyboards, dongles, small peripherals).",
  "infoUsbSpeedBullet2": "USB 3.x: much faster (disks, interfaces).",
  "infoUsbSpeedBullet3": "USB4 / Thunderbolt: very high speed (dock, eGPU, video depending on hardware).",
  "infoUsbParagraph": "In show: if a device \"disconnects\", suspect the cable (quality/standard) before the device.",
  "infoStorageSataNvmeTitle": "SATA vs NVMe",
  "infoStorageSataNvmeBullet1": "SATA SSD: good and stable, but limited (old interface).",
  "infoStorageSataNvmeBullet2": "SSD NVMe (M.2): much faster (ideal for media servers, large files).",
  "infoStorageFieldTitle": "Terrain video",
  "infoStorageFieldBullet1": "Playback of large 4K/ProRes files → NVMe recommended.",
  "infoStorageFieldBullet2": "Beware of temperature: an NVMe can throttle (slow down) if it gets too hot.",
  "infoStorageFieldBullet3": "Always test in real-life conditions before the show.",
