  "aboutNetworkChecklistTitle": "Before opening Wireshark 😄",
  "aboutNetworkFooterNote": "Indicative info (field). Depending on network hardware, IGMP/VLAN may be essential.\nObjective: keep it simple and robust.",
  "aboutNetworkCopy1": "Light network: simple, dedicated, stable aim.",
  "aboutNetworkCopy2": "VLAN = traffic separation (light vs. rest).",
  "aboutNetworkCopy3": "IGMP = indispensable if large-scale multicast sACN.",
  "aboutNetworkCopy4": "Wi-Fi = ok for troubleshooting, rarely ok for critical production.",
  "aboutNetworkChecklistCopy": "Lighting network - Checklist\n☐ Dedicated network or light VLAN\n☐ Clear IP plan (DHCP or static) + mask ok\n☐ Switch correct; loops avoided\n☐ sACN multicast: IGMP snooping ON\n☐ IGMP querier present in VLAN (if infra requires it)\n☐ Unicast troubleshooting (especially Art-Net)\n☐ Wi-Fi: avoid critical prod (jitter/losses)\n☐ Tests: stable ping + progressive load (universe)",
  "aboutNetworkToc1": "1) Objective: stable network",
  "aboutNetworkToc2": "2) Plan IP (simple)",
  "aboutNetworkToc3": "3) VLAN (separation)",
  "aboutNetworkToc4": "4) IGMP (sACN multicast)",
  "aboutNetworkToc5": "5) Wi-Fi vs. wired",
  "aboutNetworkToc6": "6) Switch: what you need",
  "aboutNetworkToc7": "7) Schematics",
  "aboutNetworkToc8": "8) Checklist",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsPill1": "Dedicated/VLAN",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsPill2": "Wired",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsPill3": "IGMP if multicast",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsParagraph": "A light network must be predictable: low loss, low jitter, simple architecture. When things go wrong, it's rarely \"the protocol\" and often the infra (switch, Wi-Fi, loops, flood).",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsCalloutTitle": "Basic rule",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsBullet1": "If you can: wired + correct switch + dedicated network (or VLAN).",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsBullet2": "If you must share: VLAN + clear rules.",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsBullet3": "sACN multicast: IGMP quickly becomes mandatory.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpParagraph": "Choose a simple, consistent strategy. Two approaches: DHCP (simple) or static (predictable). Worst case scenario: an undocumented mix.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpCalloutTitle": "Sample plan (simple)",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet1": "VLAN light: 10.10.0.0/24",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet2": "Console/PC: 10.10.0.10",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet3": "Nodes: 10.10.0.100-150",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet4": "Switch mgmt: 10.10.0.2",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubtitle": "Classic errors",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubBullet1": "Different mask (e.g. /24 vs /16) → invisible machines.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubBullet2": "Two devices same IP → random behavior.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubBullet3": "DHCP + static on same range without control → conflicts.",
  "aboutNetworkVlanParagraph": "A VLAN allows you to isolate the light from the rest (internet, video production, guests...). It avoids network noise and reduces the risk of another service breaking up your show.",
  "aboutNetworkVlanCalloutTitle": "What you earn",
  "aboutNetworkVlanBullet1": "Less parasitic traffic.",
  "aboutNetworkVlanBullet2": "Less risk (external DHCP, unwanted broadcast).",
  "aboutNetworkVlanBullet3": "Easier debugging (everything in the VLAN = light).",
  "aboutNetworkVlanSubtitle": "Attention",
  "aboutNetworkVlanSubBullet1": "A VLAN = all ports must be properly configured (access/trunk).",
  "aboutNetworkVlanSubBullet2": "If you don't master: a dedicated \"physical\" network is often simpler.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpPill1": "IGMP snooping",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpPill2": "IGMP querier",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpPill3": "Multicast flood",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpParagraph": "IGMP snooping lets the switch know which ports want which multicast. Without it, multicast can be flooded on all ports → saturation.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpCalloutTitle": "IGMP querier (simple idea)",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpBullet1": "In some networks/VLANs, a querier is required to maintain IGMP subscriptions.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpBullet2": "No quibble: depending on the switch, subscriptions expire and you see \"glitches\".",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpBullet3": "If you're on a small, dedicated network: sometimes everything works, but on a large network: it's critical.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpSubtitle": "Diagram : IGMP (idea)",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubtitle1": "Wired",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubtitle2": "Wi-Fi",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet1": "✅ Stable latency, low losses (if clean infrared).",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet2": "✅ Recommended for prod.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet3": "✅ Practical (quick setup, tablet).",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet4": "❌ Variable latency (jitter), losses, interference.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet5": "❌ Multicast sometimes poorly managed according to AP/config.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet6": "OK troubleshooting / small, non-critical setups, rarely OK in loaded show.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiCalloutTitle": "Simple rule",
  "aboutNetworkWifiBullet1": "Critical show = wired.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiBullet2": "Wi-Fi = operator comfort (UI), not main DMX/IP transport if high volume.",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchCalloutTitle": "Minimum recommended",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet1": "Correct Ethernet switch (not hub).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet2": "OK cables (RJ45, connectors).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet3": "Avoid loops (or controlled STP).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet4": "If sACN multicast: IGMP snooping.",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchSubtitle": "Managed vs unmanaged",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchSubBullet1": "Unmanaged: ok small dedicated network (simple).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchSubBullet2": "Managed: useful for VLAN/IGMP/diagnostics (large networks).",
